From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:22:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sensors: Take sensors from the host's sensors service

The HAL listed no sensors, so Android apps found no accelerometer,
compass or light sensor. It now reads the host's sensors from
deckard-sensors over /data/deckard/sensors.sock (Marathon-Deckard
docs/sensors.md): the list once at start, waiting up to 15 s for the
host because SensorService reads it only once, then the events of the
sensors Android activates, at the period Android batches. Flushes
complete at once, as nothing waits in a FIFO. When the host restarts,
the HAL reconnects and activates the same sensors again.

The service keeps registering only when deckard.stub_sensors_hal is
set, which also keeps Android's display fixed to the compositor's
rotation, and runs two binder threads, since poll() holds one.
---
 sensors/Sensors.cpp | 298 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 sensors/Sensors.h   |  33 +++++
 sensors/service.cpp |   3 +-
 3 files changed, 323 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

